#
# blaze's changes to library/ (to be kept through each bump; `harness/library.py`'s rewrite must keep these lines):
# - std/src/sys/env/unix.rs `walked`, called by `env()` and by `Command::spawn`/`exec`
#   (std/src/sys/process/unix/unix.rs) when the child gets `environ` whole: a weak call of
#   `__blaze_environ_walked`, which only blaze's sandbox interposers define, so a traced run is
#   keyed by the whole environment only when the program reads it whole. Unresolved, nothing is
#   called (v2/requests/usercode.md item 6, part 1).
# - core/src/reflect.rs (new) with its `pub mod reflect;` in core/src/lib.rs and
#   `pub use core::reflect;` in std/src/lib.rs: blaze's compile-time reflection,
#   `#![feature(blaze_comptime)]` (`Struct`, `Enum`, `Field<Base>`, `Variant<Base>`, `Marked`,
#   `Unmarked`, `fields_of`, `variants_of`, `FnItem`, `fn_info`). Every item is unstable under
#   `blaze_comptime`, its lang items are `blaze_*`, and its intrinsics (`blaze_*`, private to the
#   module) are answered only by blaze's const evaluator; nothing else in library/ refers to it,
#   so a crate without the feature sees std as the nightly's
#   (docs/v2/plan/design/comptime.md, phase 2).
# - core/src/num/arbitrary.rs (new) with its `pub mod arbitrary;` in core/src/num/mod.rs,
#   `pub use core::num::arbitrary;` in std/src/num/mod.rs, the `blaze_int_cast` intrinsic in
#   core/src/intrinsics/mod.rs and `#![blaze::arbitrary_ints]` in core/src/lib.rs: the trait
#   impls and inherent items of blaze's integers of any width (`u3`, `i24`), as blanket impls
#   over the lang-item markers `ArbitraryInt`, `ArbitrarySigned`, `IntFrom<S>` and
#   `IntTryFrom<S>`, which only blaze's trait solver answers and nothing can implement. Every
#   impl's self type or argument must be such an integer, so no other type gains an impl
#   (docs/v2/plan/design/arbitrary-ints.md).
# - core/src/blaze.rs (new) with its `pub mod blaze;` in core/src/lib.rs: blaze's own attribute
#   macros, `contract_test` (`#[rustc_builtin_macro]`, expanded by blaze's `hir-expand`), which
#   the attribute path `blaze::contract_test` names in every crate. Unstable under
#   `blaze_verify`; nothing else in library/ refers to it
#   (docs/v2/plan/design/contracts.md, part 2).
# - wasm64-blaze-wasip1 (64-bit WASI preview 1): vendor/wasip1-1.0.0/src/lib_generated.rs takes
#   every pointer and witx `size` argument of the raw imports as `usize` and imports them from
#   `wasi_snapshot_preview1` on 32-bit and `wasi_snapshot_preview1_64` on 64-bit (wasm32 is
#   unchanged); vendor/libc-0.2.191/src/wasi/mod.rs gives 64-bit WASI musl's 64-bit
#   `tm.__tm_gmtoff` (c_long), pthread type sizes and UTIME_NOW/UTIME_OMIT. Both vendored crates'
#   .cargo-checksum.json are updated.
# - wasi_rt/ (new): that target's C runtime in Rust, in place of wasi-libc (which has no
#   memory64 build): entry point, malloc, errno, environment, preopens and cwd, files,
#   directories, descriptors, clocks, single-threaded pthread, mem functions. std depends on it
#   only under cfg(all(target_os = "wasi", target_env = "p1", target_pointer_width = "64"))
#   (std/Cargo.toml) and names it with `extern crate wasi_rt;` under the same cfg
#   (std/src/lib.rs); Cargo.lock has its package and std's dependency on it. Every other
#   target's std is unchanged.
